{
  "requirement": "`Fingerprint` pairs a digest with the scheme used to compute it. Each `NodeContents`\nimplementation chooses the scheme. Freshness checks compare both fields as opaque values.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Fingerprint {\n    pub scheme: String,\n    pub value: String,\n}\n\nimpl Fingerprint {\n    pub fn new(scheme: String, value: String) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Fingerprint;\nimpl Debug for Fingerprint;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Fingerprint;\nimpl PartialEq for Fingerprint;\nimpl Serialize for Fingerprint;\nimpl Eq for Fingerprint;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover the requirement.\n\n**Freshness compares both fields as opaque values.** The check is covered by `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors]`.\n- A record with `Dependency::Node(1, fp(\"same\"))` is current while the graph content is `\"same\"`.\n- A dependency with `Fingerprint::new(\"other\", \"same\")` makes the record stale. The value matches and only the scheme differs, so the scheme is compared.\n- A dependency with `fp(\"changed\")` makes the record stale. The scheme matches and only the value differs, so the value is compared.\n- Both stale cases assert `!is_current`.\n\n**Constructor, public fields and equality.** Both tests build fingerprints with `Fingerprint::new`, and the storage test compares them through `PartialEq`.\n\n**Serialize/Deserialize.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` round-trips records through JSON files. This includes `Dependency::OutgoingEdges(..., Fingerprint::new(\"targets-v1\", \"preserved\"))`, and it asserts that the loaded dependencies equal the stored ones, so both fields survive.\n\n**Trait list and exports.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the public export inventory. It also checks that the Habeas consumer compiles against the SDK.\n\n**Derived traits.** `Clone`, `Debug`, `Eq` and `PartialEq` come from a plain `derive` on `struct[Fingerprint]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs`. I read that derive in the search results. `Fingerprint::new` is a plain field assignment. These have no conditionals or transformations of their own, so they need no separate tests.\n\nThe requirement's other statement, that each `NodeContents` implementation chooses the scheme, is covered by the `NodeContents` requirements, not here.",
